WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.560
It might thrill drivers, but countries relying
on oil exports to finance their economies

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.710
aren't happy about current price levels.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.390
For the last three months oil has been heading
steadily downhill.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:17.430
At the start of October a barrel of North
Sea Brent Crude stood at a respectable 86

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.560
dollars.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.760
By the end of November it was struggling at
57 dollars a barrel at times, though it's

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.370
stabilized for now at 60.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.580
That's causing oil producers a lot of financial
problems.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:32.250
So much so that the Organisation of Petroleum
Exporting Countries has put production cuts

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.431
high on the agenda of its latest Vienna meeting.

00:00:34.431 --> 00:00:38.010
"What we need is a fair price.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.079
And 50 is not a fair price."

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:43.440
"What is a fair price for you?

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.440
"For me?

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.140
It's a bit higher than 50."

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.140
"How much?"

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.440
"The rest is secret."

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:57.059
Economics 1-0-1: if output and hence supply
falls - prices rise.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:01.350
The US is by far the world's largest oil producer
at 14 percent of output.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.590
Russia is the second largest.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:07.810
Non-OPEC member Canada is way behind.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:13.060
Uniting 15 countries, OPEC is responsible
for 42 percent of global oil production, giving

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:15.350
it the main sway over pricing.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:20.500
The organisation's most important single member
is Saudi Arabia, which alone pumps 13 percent

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.020
of the world's crude supply.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.119
But not everyone's happy about the idea of
falling supply and rising expense.

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:30.590
US President Trump has no interest in high
oil prices.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:33.400
He appealed to OPEC on Twitter not to cut
output.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.490
At the same time though Non-OPEC member Russia
said is is ready to implement output cuts

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.050
-- as has OPEC heavyweight Saudi Arabia.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:02:08.479
The talk in Vienna

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:21.930
is 
of

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:57.349
a one

00:02:57.349 --> 00:03:59.010
percent

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:04.609
cut in production.

